  ('34b09cd6-88c0-5244-aadc-18aee521bcb3', '5e8c9edf-2894-5eff-93fc-61960c94ec0a', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Three elements of ONE programme (Stanley R. Mickelsen Safeguard Complex) in two adjacent North Dakota counties, sharing an era, a squadron lineage and a popular name. They are distinct structures on distinct parcels with COMPLETELY DIVERGENT present status: the MSR was deactivated in 1976 and sold twice, PARCS is a currently operating Space Force installation, RSL-3 is privately owned and toured. Collapsing them would produce a single record that is simultaneously abandoned, operational and a tourist attraction. This is exactly the ''two genuinely distinct sites in the same complex'' case.'),
  ('34b09cd6-88c0-5244-aadc-18aee521bcb3', '979fa4f1-e453-5e7f-a82a-58a9ea757139', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Three elements of ONE programme (Stanley R. Mickelsen Safeguard Complex) in two adjacent North Dakota counties, sharing an era, a squadron lineage and a popular name. They are distinct structures on distinct parcels with COMPLETELY DIVERGENT present status: the MSR was deactivated in 1976 and sold twice, PARCS is a currently operating Space Force installation, RSL-3 is privately owned and toured. Collapsing them would produce a single record that is simultaneously abandoned, operational and a tourist attraction. This is exactly the ''two genuinely distinct sites in the same complex'' case.'),
  ('5e8c9edf-2894-5eff-93fc-61960c94ec0a', '979fa4f1-e453-5e7f-a82a-58a9ea757139', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Three elements of ONE programme (Stanley R. Mickelsen Safeguard Complex) in two adjacent North Dakota counties, sharing an era, a squadron lineage and a popular name. They are distinct structures on distinct parcels with COMPLETELY DIVERGENT present status: the MSR was deactivated in 1976 and sold twice, PARCS is a currently operating Space Force installation, RSL-3 is privately owned and toured. Collapsing them would produce a single record that is simultaneously abandoned, operational and a tourist attraction. This is exactly the ''two genuinely distinct sites in the same complex'' case.'),
  ('a8468a29-43e6-570f-801c-54ed026e2546', '11aaea4c-ac65-5ace-b4c3-5543d782bc6e', 'PART-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'CONTAINMENT, NOT IDENTITY. Oscar-Zero and November-33 are members of the 321st SMW/MG field that RES-046 describes as a population. Merging them would erase the one fact that makes RES-045 interesting — that these two parcels were preserved while the population around them was demolished under treaty. Recorded as a containment edge instead.'),
  ('6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', '4a9d6fb0-5146-51e6-991f-c635794cefe1', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Two ''Denver'' candidates from two beats that searched blind to each other, one a real earth-covered federal structure with an NRHP listing, the other a non-existent claimed base under an airport terminal 25 miles away. Named explicitly because an automated name-similarity merge would join them and produce the single most damaging record the register could publish.'),
  ('4b87bd09-0843-5042-9b46-a7c6008d005b', '5b9e31bf-a8fa-5b3f-878d-a3ef7d7e2fdb', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Bothell''s FRC is reported BUILT ON a refurbished decommissioned Nike missile site; BA-79 is a Nike site in Maryland occupied by the Civil Air Patrol. Shared typology and shared programme heritage, nothing else. Likewise RES-007 Olney, where a Nike installation features in the site''s garbled chronology.'),
  ('b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', '650fa298-2703-5ae9-8fd5-d89c62f0e4fb', 'PARENT-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'RES-012 is a SYSTEM-scope record whose extension is exactly the five member stations. It is NOT a sixth site and its sources are literally the same source objects as its members''. It is retained because the chain-level claim (that these five form one programme) is itself a proposition worth grading — but any downstream process that counts six candidates here with independent evidence at each has multiplied one researcher''s page by six.'),
  ('b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', '243defd8-e4e2-5113-9a6d-2a6c31519ab2', 'PARENT-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'RES-012 is a SYSTEM-scope record whose extension is exactly the five member stations. It is NOT a sixth site and its sources are literally the same source objects as its members''. It is retained because the chain-level claim (that these five form one programme) is itself a proposition worth grading — but any downstream process that counts six candidates here with independent evidence at each has multiplied one researcher''s page by six.'),
  ('b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', '6aee9e0f-3053-5271-9e7d-548ec186fc98', 'PARENT-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'RES-012 is a SYSTEM-scope record whose extension is exactly the five member stations. It is NOT a sixth site and its sources are literally the same source objects as its members''. It is retained because the chain-level claim (that these five form one programme) is itself a proposition worth grading — but any downstream process that counts six candidates here with independent evidence at each has multiplied one researcher''s page by six.'),
  ('b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', '83f6fea7-1527-5fc1-8842-0253c0403aa3', 'PARENT-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'RES-012 is a SYSTEM-scope record whose extension is exactly the five member stations. It is NOT a sixth site and its sources are literally the same source objects as its members''. It is retained because the chain-level claim (that these five form one programme) is itself a proposition worth grading — but any downstream process that counts six candidates here with independent evidence at each has multiplied one researcher''s page by six.'),
  ('b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', 'c388c40c-7b18-54c3-9e6d-6d640b3e8478', 'PARENT-OF', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'RES-012 is a SYSTEM-scope record whose extension is exactly the five member stations. It is NOT a sixth site and its sources are literally the same source objects as its members''. It is retained because the chain-level claim (that these five form one programme) is itself a proposition worth grading — but any downstream process that counts six candidates here with independent evidence at each has multiplied one researcher''s page by six.'),
  ('231a7cbb-2895-52cf-89c5-c1dad8ab92b8', 'b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'The comms beat caught its OWN search-tool conflation here and recorded it as a finding against its process rather than against a source: a query naming several candidate sites returned the Netcong CLUI entry among Project Office material and the summary presented them as one set. Netcong is AT&T''s underground network operations centre in northern New Jersey with no troposcatter role reported; the chain is five mid-Atlantic troposcatter stations. An erroneously admitted sixth member would have inflated the chain''s apparent membership and diluted every genuine member''s grade. This resolution upholds the exclusion.'),
  ('4a9d6fb0-5146-51e6-991f-c635794cefe1', 'f8fa3c7f-7185-5a18-ba9b-c0bf5cf2920a', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'NOT merged as ENTITIES — one is a site claim, the other a non-located enumeration — but they SHARE A SINGLE LINEAGE TERMINUS and their independent-origin counts must therefore be pooled, not summed. Treating them as two supporting sources for a common thesis double-counts one 1995 lecture. This is the distinction between entity resolution and lineage resolution and it is why the two must be done as separate passes. | LINEAGES POOLED, NOT SUMMED: same single terminus (N-SCHNEIDER); see the citation graph.'),
  ('1be32b23-ba20-52e7-bef1-e6ec84be9e3e', '7afb161b-09a4-57d1-9be8-667dc5cbc89f', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Four converted Atlas launch sites in four states sharing a typology, a conversion narrative and much of a marketing vocabulary (see N-20THCENT). Distinct parcels, distinct squadrons, distinct owners. The shared vocabulary is a LINEAGE fact about the descriptions, not an entity fact about the places.'),
  ('1be32b23-ba20-52e7-bef1-e6ec84be9e3e', 'bb184b91-1580-52d2-a380-df14986e1fc6', 'DISTINCT-FROM', 'sweep-01-ingest', 'Four converted Atlas launch sites in four states sharing a typology, a conversion narrative and much of a marketing vocabulary (see N-20THCENT). Distinct parcels, distinct squadrons, distinct owners. The shared vocabulary is a LINEAGE fact about the descriptions, not an entity fact about the places.'),
