values
  ('d4cff3cc-fa14-516a-aa11-b9ebf05484fd', '6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', 'place_name_only', 'Jefferson County, Colorado (Lakewood), on the federally owned Denver Federal Center', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Within the Denver Federal Center campus, Lakewood, Colorado. Reported as an earth-covered structure under approximately three feet of soil, 36,000 sq ft over two levels. | basis: Named campus and municipality only, from search summaries of GSA and History Colorado pages. I hold no receipted coordinate, no parcel identifier and no NRHP reference number. I have not fabricated a lat/lon and none is supplied.'),
  ('32014e2a-66bc-5e83-9286-02de4dc6af97', '4d5e2d74-749b-5c63-ae1a-f5535f9a4cd4', 'place_name_only', 'Denton County, Texas', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Denton, Texas. Reported as two below-grade levels of approximately 25,000 sq ft each behind a 13-ton blast door. | basis: Municipality only, from search summaries. No receipted coordinate, parcel or address. No lat/lon supplied because I hold none.'),
  ('a38eb2b3-1b88-5259-8e51-4ea99b23e7bd', '4b87bd09-0843-5042-9b46-a7c6008d005b', 'place_name_only', 'Snohomish County, Washington (reported as 228th Street Southwest)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. Snohomish County, Washington, near Bothell, reported on 228th Street Southwest on a former Nike missile site. Reported footprint 120 by 140 feet. | basis: A named street in a named county, from a search summary of local journalism. This is a street name, not a receipted address or parcel, and I have not converted it to a coordinate. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('020737af-0320-5c7f-9661-50b0d9396c69', '808e73e9-ce30-58f6-9724-92286c4b7f1b', 'place_name_only', 'Middlesex County, Massachusetts (Maynard)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Maynard, Massachusetts, reported as approximately 20 miles from Boston. | basis: Municipality and an approximate distance-from-Boston, from search summaries. No receipted coordinate or parcel. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('a05b8604-7850-5380-9c34-958e8ffc53d3', '89596351-771b-5639-bb3b-02524967cff7', 'place_name_only', 'Thomas County, Georgia (Thomasville), reported on South Broad Street or a South-side parcel', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Thomasville, Georgia. Reported as a 37,734 sq ft subterranean protected facility on a 38-acre site. | basis: Municipality only, from search summaries. The ''38-acre site'' and square footage are reported figures I have not receipted. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('03ef4d92-aba5-5592-bc01-ed5f6fe597e4', 'e78961a9-ffa5-5288-8c4b-7616f0174062', 'place_name_only', 'Sonoma County, California', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: claimed-only. Sonoma County, California, on or adjacent to the former Naval Auxiliary Air Station Santa Rosa. The commonly cited Chanate Road association did not survive my searching and I do not carry it forward as established. | basis: A former installation name and a county. I could not confirm the specific parcel, and the Chanate Road attribution I searched for was not corroborated by any result. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('eb18e9b7-6c02-5b58-829d-c947e83b32ae', 'eb62ea03-73c8-596b-adf7-d5bdf3417a52', 'place_name_only', 'Montgomery County, Maryland (Olney), reported on Georgia Avenue', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Olney, Montgomery County, Maryland, in the northern Washington suburbs. | basis: Municipality and county from search summaries. No receipted parcel or coordinate. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('69c180f9-85b2-53cf-97a4-778b1cd13fe6', 'e3259c83-d879-5f2c-9daa-d5c4ea25d8c8', 'place_name_only', 'Warren County, Virginia (Front Royal)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. Front Royal, Warren County, Virginia, on the property now occupied by the Smithsonian Conservation Biology Institute. | basis: A named, currently operating, publicly identifiable institution occupies the property, so the parcel is unambiguous even though I hold no receipted coordinate. No lat/lon supplied because I have not resolved one.'),
  ('7fc8b580-e903-5ac1-ad71-0299fb0ba217', '17f6ad10-3b2b-5576-b8f3-ba5b7c027b59', 'place_name_only', 'Washington County / Frederick County, Maryland — reported on South Mountain between Middletown and Rohrersville, near the Appalachian Trail', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. Lambs Knoll, on the South Mountain ridge in western Maryland, close to the Appalachian Trail corridor. | basis: A named, mapped, publicly accessible topographic summit with an existing public communications tower. The named place is unambiguous; the specific structure and its extent are not. No lat/lon supplied because I have not receipted one and the summit name is sufficient to locate the search.'),
  ('122eeaee-a944-5a49-a3f4-bc5a3dd9280d', 'a0f0e46e-679e-5f23-896f-50b31211ade8', 'place_name_only', 'Calhoun County, Michigan (Battle Creek)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. Battle Creek, Michigan, on Washington Avenue. A large, conspicuous, above-ground historic building complex. | basis: A named, currently operating, NRHP-associated federal building complex in a named city, from GSA and news search summaries. Unambiguous as a place. No lat/lon supplied.'),
  ('43ab16d2-b8f0-5fe7-8213-8be7ac5598bf', 'f788b0db-40db-5c10-8a22-fed8155cec28', 'place_name_only', 'Adams County, Pennsylvania, near Blue Ridge Summit and Fountaindale, with associated works in Maryland', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Inside Raven Rock Mountain, Adams County, Pennsylvania, reported as about 14 km east of Waynesboro, Pennsylvania and about 10 km north-northeast of Camp David. | basis: Named mountain, county and bearings-and-distances from two named public landmarks, from search summaries. I hold no receipted coordinate. No lat/lon supplied, and for an active facility the register''s own rule against manufacturing precise pins from imprecise evidence applies with extra force.'),
  ('37dd5c95-e0ce-5a12-b388-45d54df74254', 'b3b873ae-2bce-5f49-8aeb-0c999fbbfb68', 'place_name_only', 'Multi-state: Washington County MD; Loudoun County VA; Albemarle County VA; Buckingham County VA; Chatham County NC', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. A north–south chain of five hardened stations running from the Bear Pond Mountains northwest of Hagerstown, Maryland, through Short Hill Mountain in western Loudoun County, Virginia; Peters Mountain roughly 16 miles east of Charlottesville, Virginia; Spears Mountain roughly 11 miles west of the town of Buckingham, Virginia; to a site off Big Hole Road in Chatham County, North Carolina, south of Chapel Hill. | basis: Verbal placement only, taken from search summaries of the CLUI Land Use Database and coldwar-c4i.net. No coordinate was resolved in this session and none is asserted. The landform names above are the strongest locators the sources supply and are sufficient to drive a parcel or HTMC query.'),
  ('ce294b1d-b924-5d0b-a93d-95393c9bd0f1', '650fa298-2703-5ae9-8fd5-d89c62f0e4fb', 'place_name_only', 'Loudoun County, Virginia', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. On the ridge of Short Hill Mountain in western Loudoun County, Virginia, in the ''Between the Hills'' area near Hillsboro and Lovettsville, north of Harpers Ferry. | basis: Named landform from CLUI and Loudoun County land-use reporting. No coordinate resolved; the Loudoun County parcel record and the 2016 commission-permit file would both give an exact one and neither was reachable.'),
  ('ea899764-82b6-567f-846d-b2222892ccdd', '243defd8-e4e2-5113-9a6d-2a6c31519ab2', 'place_name_only', 'Chatham County, North Carolina', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Off Big Hole Road in rural Chatham County, North Carolina, south of Chapel Hill and near Pittsboro. The southern terminus of the Project Office chain. | basis: Named road and county from CLUI and Indy Week reporting. No coordinate resolved. The road name is itself a local artefact of the construction and is a strong locator for a parcel query.'),
  ('eca5af00-ff47-5113-8272-09688e3ef686', '6aee9e0f-3053-5271-9e7d-548ec186fc98', 'place_name_only', 'Washington County, Maryland', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. On a mountaintop in the Bear Pond Mountains, northwest of Hagerstown, Maryland, near the Pennsylvania line. The northern terminus of the Project Office chain. | basis: Named mountain range and county from coldwar-c4i.net as relayed in a search summary. No coordinate resolved.'),
  ('2bd08c7c-dbb0-54db-ac18-328b76876434', '83f6fea7-1527-5fc1-8842-0253c0403aa3', 'place_name_only', 'Albemarle County, Virginia', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. On Peters Mountain, roughly 16 miles east of Charlottesville, Albemarle County, Virginia, on or near Peters Mountain Road. | basis: Named landform, road and distance-from-Charlottesville, from CLUI and coldwar-c4i.net via search summaries. No coordinate resolved.'),
  ('43e57e94-9ad0-5122-b164-b9a919a6f5c9', 'c388c40c-7b18-54c3-9e6d-6d640b3e8478', 'place_name_only', 'Buckingham County, Virginia', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Atop Spears Mountain, roughly 11 miles west of the town of Buckingham, Buckingham County, Virginia, near the geographic centre of the state. | basis: Named mountain, county and distance-from-town, from coldwar-c4i.net and CLUI via search summaries. No coordinate resolved.'),
  ('41af3957-b6bf-53f8-8b3d-8cf036f3eeee', '231a7cbb-2895-52cf-89c5-c1dad8ab92b8', 'place_name_only', 'Morris County, New Jersey (Netcong borough / Roxbury township area)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. On a hilltop in or adjoining Netcong borough, Morris County, New Jersey, in the general area of AT&T''s later Bedminster and Basking Ridge centres. | basis: Borough name from CLUI and from the operator''s own facility page. No coordinate resolved. Note the naming conflict: CLUI calls it Netcong, the operator calls it Roxbury — adjoining municipalities — which is itself an entity-resolution hazard worth recording.'),
  ('d84b1830-8dff-5870-b47b-b3e51cbdbbfa', 'c9265e0a-b364-5090-92cf-f01df8cd3322', 'place_name_only', 'Burt County, Nebraska', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. On Highway 51 at Lyons, Burt County, Nebraska, roughly 90 miles north of Offutt Air Force Base. | basis: Street address (1650 Hwy 51, Lyons NE) appeared in a search summary of a commercial real-estate listing. This is a postal address, not a surveyed coordinate, and I did not resolve it. Recorded because a street address is a far better handle for a parcel query than a guessed decimal degree.'),
  ('cb995c9d-82a3-54c2-89eb-cb5d9a59c881', 'b0578b45-867a-5761-8ba1-55d30476668b', 'place_name_only', 'Boone County, Iowa', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. In farmland north of Des Moines, in the Boone, Iowa area, with a microwave relay tower on the surface. | basis: County and general placement from the CLUI entry and the operator''s material. The operator gives a Des Moines business address (3101 Ingersoll Ave) which is an office, not the facility. No facility coordinate resolved and none asserted.'),
  ('26e698cf-f20f-50b8-9ee4-8a6ad00adf8e', '1fe2ae68-6caf-5734-9cc7-21713b8566c3', 'place_name_only', 'District of Columbia', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. In the Tenleytown neighbourhood of northwest Washington DC, near the highest natural elevation in the District, in the vicinity of 41st Street NW and Wisconsin Avenue. One search summary gives a street address of 4623 41st Street NW. | basis: Neighbourhood and street address from search summaries of DC Historic Sites and coldwar-c4i.net. The address was not resolved and one search summary explicitly corrected a different address I had proposed, so treat it as indicative. No coordinate asserted.'),
  ('e28dfe16-49d2-5242-9491-c15d15e4d497', '1f48ad29-4020-50b4-8953-b6dbc1ba3d9b', 'place_name_only', 'Hampshire County, Massachusetts (Hadley), on and under Bare Mountain', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. Bare Mountain, Hadley, Massachusetts, within the Holyoke Range. Reported as two underground storeys totalling approximately 40,000 sq ft designed for 135 people. | basis: A named mountain in a named town, with a currently operating institutional occupant. Unambiguous as a place. No lat/lon supplied because I have not receipted one.'),
  ('8e859253-79f7-5c5e-b5eb-d403f4319c0d', 'a7219ff5-7b09-5d66-9ee0-c3d2b1b64142', 'place_name_only', 'Multiple Missouri counties, including Maries County (Brinktown), Lafayette County (Dover), Saline County (Slater), Ste. Genevieve County (Lawrenceton)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Rural sites across central and eastern Missouri along the AT&T Long Lines Kansas City–St Louis and Kansas City–east microwave routes, each identified in the underlying source by an FCC Antenna Structure Registration number and by named township. | basis: Named towns and counties from search summaries of Garrett Fuller''s site-by-site blog. No coordinates resolved. Note that FCC ASR records carry surveyed coordinates for every registered structure, which makes this the one candidate class on the beat where exact locations are cheaply and authoritatively obtainable — from a corpus I could not reach. | SCOPE: population — must never be rendered as a pin.'),
  ('20a58ec0-24a5-5056-872c-baab96de14c3', 'dd70c345-a053-514f-bdc7-361e22b1e5b9', 'place_name_only', 'Rio Arriba County, New Mexico; Jicarilla Apache Nation lands adjoin the claimed location', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: claimed-only. Archuleta Mesa, north of the village of Dulce, New Mexico, on or adjacent to Jicarilla Apache Nation land near the Colorado state line. I hold no receipted coordinate. The claim itself has never been given consistent coordinates by its own sources. | basis: Place name only, from search summaries. No parcel, no PLSS description, no coordinate was retrieved. I have not invented one.'),
  ('577c5658-734e-51c2-a54a-de3c37e74848', '4a9d6fb0-5146-51e6-991f-c635794cefe1', 'place_name_only', 'City and County of Denver, Colorado (the airport parcel lies in Denver, surrounded by Adams County)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Beneath the Jeppesen Terminal and concourses, Denver International Airport, Denver, Colorado. | basis: Named airport and municipality only, from search summaries. No receipted coordinate, no parcel identifier, no plan sheet. None invented.'),
  ('e9743583-3af8-58e1-b15a-f11d18e2aafb', '4ab062f1-f9a5-52a9-8b18-640c3cc94cfb', 'non_located', null, 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: none. The research programme is located at Los Alamos Scientific Laboratory, New Mexico. The claimed transcontinental network has no location and never has had one - no source in the lineage gives a portal, an alignment, or a coordinate. | basis: The programme is institutionally located by its report series. The claimed network is non-located in the BES 10.4 sense - documented as a claim, coordinates genuinely never asserted. No coordinate invented.'),
  ('a5fd82e4-f026-5f3e-a26f-89f6f2dc7061', '194af68e-782e-590a-877c-71d712ce52df', 'place_name_only', 'City and County of Los Angeles, California', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: approximate. A vacant lot at 518 North Hill Street, downtown Los Angeles, on the old Banning property overlooking Sunset Boulevard, Spring Street and North Broadway; the claimed ''Key Room'' was placed beneath Broadway and Second Street. The Fort Moore Hill site has since been substantially regraded and built over. | basis: A named street address reported in contemporaneous newspaper coverage, retrieved as a search summary. I hold no receipted coordinate and no parcel record. None invented.'),
  ('e76d07df-414d-5cf8-9c10-3fd52fa1c462', '968fb226-746a-50b0-80e8-1c101472ff70', 'place_name_only', 'San Bernardino County, California; BLM Needles Field Office administers the surrounding claims', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Kokoweef Peak, eastern Mojave Desert, San Bernardino County, California. Real, mapped, and the site of continuously worked mining claims. The claimed cavern''s location within the peak has never been consistently specified - Dorr''s affidavit reportedly does not name Kokoweef Peak or Crystal Cave at all. | basis: Named peak and county from search summaries, plus a BLM lode claim (''RAINBOW'', 20.66 acres, San Bernardino County, located 2007, serial reported as CAMC289854) surfaced through a third-party mirror of BLM MLRS. I did not resolve the claim record at BLM and hold no receipted coordinate.'),
  ('976652fe-862f-5887-aa8a-5fa5212dc8d6', '1b90e581-73d9-5d5c-b8a1-56e1be44a233', 'place_name_only', 'Kittitas County, Washington - claimed as private rural land approximately nine miles west of Ellensburg', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: claimed-only. Claimed as rural private property roughly nine miles west of Ellensburg, Kittitas County, Washington, in the Manastash Ridge area. No parcel has ever been identified and organised ground searches have not located any such feature. | basis: A claimed distance and direction from a named town, given on air by a person whose existence in the county record has not been established. I hold no coordinate, no parcel and no receipted record, and I have not invented any.'),
  ('f1ecd0ce-3b30-5e1d-842a-92864d99601b', 'c18f2c4a-9dce-5341-b5f7-f5fbe5a3c130', 'place_name_only', 'Columbia County, New York (the facility named in the text); the document itself is non-located', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. The text names an underground facility ''near the town of Hudson'', New York, described as a nuclear hideout used by large American corporations for records storage and substitute headquarters. That describes a real class of facility and, on its face, a real one. I did not establish which specific site. | basis: A place name given inside a document I have not read, reported in search summaries. No coordinate, no parcel, none invented.'),
  ('ed16e99d-7608-5385-bd17-0ff3a5b47ec9', '07bdd969-9e9b-5567-bdd1-1d0c3de3b705', 'place_name_only', 'Greene and Montgomery Counties, Ohio; Wright-Patterson AFB, Area B', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Area B, Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, near Dayton, Ohio. The Library of Congress HAER survey documents a Building 18 in Area B at the northeast corner of C and Fifth Streets, identified as the Power Plant Laboratory Complex. | basis: A named installation and a street intersection given in a HAER survey title retrieved as a search summary. loc.gov is egress-blocked from this container. No coordinate invented.'),
  ('5608a256-5bea-5de6-a544-b176a32ae19e', 'f8fa3c7f-7185-5a18-ba9b-c0bf5cf2920a', 'non_located', null, 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: none. None. In thirty years of circulation the claim has never been accompanied by coordinates, a site list, or a single named facility that can be checked. That absence is a property of the claim, not of my search. | basis: Non-located in the BES 10.4 sense. No coordinate exists to record and none invented.'),
  ('338c370e-51de-5bbe-ba9e-22d1aa903431', 'dd705501-7987-5de7-a4c2-8f782734570b', 'place_name_only', 'Loudoun and Clarke Counties, Virginia, near Bluemont', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Near Bluemont, Virginia, on the Loudoun/Clarke county line. The facility is federally acknowledged and its location is public. | basis: Named locality only, from search summaries. No receipted coordinate; the register holds this site elsewhere at band A and I am not the source for its geometry.'),
  ('f94ede9a-46fb-55a3-911f-741ae906d47e', '8e5d217e-9e41-522c-9b4b-50881a1f7d75', 'non_located', null, 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: none. None. The ''detention camps'' list that circulates has never resolved to a set of checkable parcels; where individual sites are named they are typically existing, publicly known federal installations. | basis: Non-located. No coordinate exists to record and none invented.'),
  ('988a8014-48a0-5793-97ad-ed57e6b33b1d', '2483182c-d84a-5345-9c32-7ac28cd2e006', 'non_located', null, 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: none. None. The claim asserts a worldwide cavern system with no located instance. | basis: Non-located. No coordinate invented.'),
  ('50204e28-bf97-5fcc-8f31-720cb07e8a50', '34b09cd6-88c0-5244-aadc-18aee521bcb3', 'place_name_only', 'Cavalier County, North Dakota', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Near Nekoma, Cavalier County, North Dakota. Town-level only. | basis: Town name appears consistently across every search snippet. I have no coordinate from any source I saw and did not derive one. No parcel identifier retrieved.'),
  ('d4a89eb0-d397-5a84-ae61-3df979a37b4b', '5e8c9edf-2894-5eff-93fc-61960c94ec0a', 'place_name_only', 'Pembina County, North Dakota (near Cavalier / Concrete)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Near Cavalier and the hamlet of Concrete, Pembina County, North Dakota. | basis: Place names appear in search snippets (spaceforce.mil fact sheet, Cold War Tourist page title ''Cavalier Air Force Station, Concrete, ND''). No coordinate retrieved; none derived.'),
  ('8216dda7-ceb8-5eee-bd94-1c856910807a', '979fa4f1-e453-5e7f-a82a-58a9ea757139', 'place_name_only', 'Cavalier County, North Dakota', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Cavalier County, North Dakota, one of four dispersed RSL sites around the Mickelsen complex. | basis: County-level from search snippets only. No coordinate retrieved. Atlas Obscura and a tour operator''s own site both exist for this location and either would give a coordinate if fetchable.'),
  ('c82e1741-f1e9-5030-aa88-6b1d2f722043', '1be32b23-ba20-52e7-bef1-e6ec84be9e3e', 'place_name_only', 'Town of Lewis, Essex County, New York', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Town of Lewis, Essex County, New York — one of twelve Atlas F sites ringing the former Plattsburgh AFB, seven of them inside the Adirondack Park Blue Line. | basis: Town and county from search snippets (Adirondack Explorer, themilitarystandard site page title, Adirondack Architectural Heritage tour listing). No coordinate retrieved. Wikimapia carries one and is CROWD-EDITED — a lead only, per P-04.'),
  ('28b2acb9-cc75-592a-9283-f43b760e9236', '7afb161b-09a4-57d1-9be8-667dc5cbc89f', 'place_name_only', 'Cloud County, Kansas (near Concordia)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: claimed-only. Near Concordia, Cloud County, Kansas. | basis: The coordinate pair appeared inside a search-result summary that was itself summarising what is almost certainly a Wikipedia infobox. I did not fetch the page, did not verify it against a parcel, and have not checked it against the county boundary. It is recorded as claimed-only and MUST NOT be rendered as a pin. Anyone using it should treat it as a lead.'),
  ('a594203e-5990-597a-8834-a792989b1da5', 'bb184b91-1580-52d2-a380-df14986e1fc6', 'place_name_only', 'Shawnee County, Kansas (variously given as Dover or Keene, ~25 miles west of Topeka)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Near Dover / Keene, Shawnee County, Kansas, roughly 25 miles west of Topeka. | basis: Place names from search snippets, which disagree between ''Dover'' and ''Keene'' — two nearby localities. RoadsideAmerica indexes it under Shawnee County. No coordinate retrieved; none derived. The Dover/Keene split is itself a small entity-resolution problem worth recording rather than smoothing over.'),
  ('08450136-5788-5827-b98f-c158d5ffc8ce', '3efe1867-86a3-5489-8335-66301349c0f0', 'place_name_only', 'Elbert County (Complex 2C, south of Elizabeth) and Arapahoe County (Complex 2B, north of Deer Trail), Colorado', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Six former Titan I complexes remain in Colorado: four on the former Lowry Bombing and Gunnery Range east of Aurora, one north of Deer Trail, one south of Elizabeth. | basis: Distribution taken from a search summary of the CDPHE Titan 1 page and an enthusiast site. No coordinates retrieved. NOTE A DESIGNATION CONFLICT I DID NOT RESOLVE: the state agency material is summarised using ''Complex 2B / 2C'' while enthusiast and forum sources use Air Force-style ''724-A'' through ''724-F''. Two designation systems for the same six objects is a live IDENTITY problem and I have not … | SPLIT REQUIRED before any member is rendered (two complexes in one record).'),
  ('1a8bfeb0-9fb0-5e85-9d7a-47be6bfe1d19', 'b8749dde-90b2-5cb0-82e3-af557010eaf8', 'place_name_only', 'Van Buren County, Arkansas (Southside, just north of Damascus, which straddles Van Buren and Faulkner counties)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Southside, Van Buren County, Arkansas, north of Damascus, off US-65. Reported as behind a barn on private land with a locked gate. | basis: Place description assembled from search snippets (Encyclopedia of Arkansas, a visitor blog, a Waze POI title). No coordinate retrieved and none derived. A Waze POI exists, which is crowd-sourced — a lead only.'),
  ('1d173f08-7ae0-5ad2-b8ec-281e2944f3ee', '5b9e31bf-a8fa-5b3f-878d-a3ef7d7e2fdb', 'place_name_only', 'Baltimore County, Maryland (Granite), ~30 miles northwest of Baltimore', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Granite, Baltimore County, Maryland. | basis: Place name from multiple search snippets. No coordinate retrieved. Ed Thelen''s Nike register carries site coordinates for the full population and is the obvious source; I could not reach it.'),
  ('f76b790e-dcf0-5bbe-afe1-82f4e1049183', 'a8468a29-43e6-570f-801c-54ed026e2546', 'place_name_only', 'Griggs County, North Dakota (near Cooperstown)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Near Cooperstown, Griggs County, North Dakota. Two separate parcels: the Oscar-Zero missile alert facility and the November-33 launch facility. | basis: Place names from the State Historical Society of North Dakota''s own site pages and a SAH Archipedia entry, both via search snippets. No coordinate retrieved.'),
  ('07390a7c-537c-56a5-90d1-0b3ed87e0520', '11aaea4c-ac65-5ace-b4c3-5543d782bc6e', 'place_name_only', 'Northeastern North Dakota — Grand Forks, Walsh, Nelson, Cavalier and adjoining counties', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. A dispersed field of 150 launch facilities and 15 missile alert facilities across northeastern North Dakota. This is a POPULATION, not a point, and must never be rendered as a pin. | basis: Regional description from search snippets. No individual site coordinates retrieved. §10.3 applies: a precise pin manufactured from imprecise evidence would be the register performing citogenesis at the interface layer. | SCOPE: population — must never be rendered as a pin.'),
  ('d2d3ab89-2619-5e78-86ce-d5e4be8b501a', '1be2860c-bb6f-5533-9464-e9a84e3600a2', 'place_name_only', 'Chaves County, New Mexico (and adjoining counties — the 579th ring extends beyond a single county)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: claimed-only. One of twelve 579th SMS Atlas F sites in a ring around Roswell, New Mexico. WHICH ONE IS UNKNOWN TO ME. | basis: I could not determine which of the twelve site designations corresponds to the converted property. Enthusiast pages exist for 579-1 through at least 579-12, and I saw several in results, but nothing tied a designation to the owner named in the news coverage. I am recording the ambiguity rather than picking one. No coordinate. | SCOPE: population — must never be rendered as a pin. | Site identity unresolved among twelve 579th SMS sites; must not be pinned.'),
  ('18852a34-382f-52b2-af13-5be6fca69823', 'd85134b6-1307-5c93-83f8-3ffd020bd737', 'place_name_only', 'Laramie County and adjoining counties, Wyoming (dispersed around F.E. Warren AFB, Cheyenne)', 'narrative-description', 'sweep-01-ingest', true, 'precision as carried by resolved.json: regional. Dispersed complexes around F.E. Warren AFB near Cheyenne, Wyoming. A population of nine launchers per squadron across three complexes. | basis: Organisational description from search snippets. No coordinates, no individual complex locations retrieved. Population, not point. | SCOPE: population — must never be rendered as a pin.')
insert into core.claim
  (claim_id, claim_text, entity_id, cluster_key, first_appearance_document_id, first_appearance_date, first_appearance_confidence)
values
  ('b830eb08-c9a9-5d8f-b125-afbfb0d131e7', 'No source reaching me agrees on when the Maynard facility was built, and the disagreement is unresolved in the public record as indexed.', '808e73e9-ce30-58f6-9724-92286c4b7f1b', null, null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('c33ecc76-876e-571c-a0af-e19cee661c03', 'The publicly circulating chronology of the Olney site is internally incoherent and no source reaching me reconciles it.', 'eb62ea03-73c8-596b-adf7-d5bdf3417a52', null, null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('7c6c4342-3b0c-5e9e-b0b8-5454b4ac91aa', 'The Dulce underground-base claim first appears with Paul Bennewitz in Albuquerque, 1979-1980, and acquires its canonical multi-level-facility form through Thomas Allen LeVesque writing as ''Jason Bishop III'' (1989) and the ''Thomas Castello'' persona (c. 1987-1991), then through Bruce Alan Walton writing as ''BRANTON''.', 'dd70c345-a053-514f-bdc7-361e22b1e5b9', null, null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('171a31d2-8e63-5af4-8a23-02f05b00fd7c', 'The specific claim of a multi-level hardened complex beneath DIA - ''eight levels'', a ''4.5 square mile underground city'', an ''88.5 square mile base'' - originates with Phil Schneider and was propagated in print by Alex Christopher, whose ''Pandora''s Box'' appeared in 1993 and whose ''Pandora''s Box II: The Denver International Airport Story'' followed in 1996.', '4a9d6fb0-5146-51e6-991f-c635794cefe1', 'N-SCHNEIDER', null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('46a59059-7124-5000-a5e9-2015195ea9db', 'The claim first appears in the Los Angeles Times of 29 January 1934, in an article by Jean Bosquet headed ''Lizard People''s Catacomb City Hunted'', reporting the assertions of mining engineer G. Warren Shufelt.', '194af68e-782e-590a-877c-71d712ce52df', null, null, '1934-01-29', 'inferred'),
  ('5eea95aa-4af4-5ccc-9ac4-2afaf4457f33', 'The claim originates in a notarised affidavit by Earl Dorr, executed in Pasadena on 16 November 1934, first published in the California Mining Journal, November 1940.', '968fb226-746a-50b0-80e8-1c101472ff70', null, null, '1934-11-16', 'inferred'),
  ('e39011a7-de0c-566a-9b9f-89030857eec9', 'The claim first appears on the Coast to Coast AM broadcast of 21 February 1997, from a caller identifying himself as Mel Waters, with a second appearance on 24 February 1997 and further appearances in 2000 and 2002.', '1b90e581-73d9-5d5c-b8a1-56e1be44a233', null, null, '1997-02-21', 'inferred'),
  ('9bcf6cd2-5328-588b-bed8-5c6f2b2b0bae', 'The ''Report from Iron Mountain'' was written by Leonard C. Lewin, published by Dial Press in 1967, and admitted by Lewin to be a satirical fabrication in the New York Times Book Review of 19 March 1972.', 'c18f2c4a-9dce-5341-b5f7-f5fbe5a3c130', null, null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('386b11bf-1de5-5bff-a046-d8a8a82f6407', 'The most-cited documentary artifact behind the claim is a letter of 28 March 1975 from Senator Barry Goldwater to Shlomo Arnon, stating that Goldwater had roughly a decade earlier sought access to the building at Wright-Patterson where Air Force UFO material was held and had been refused, and that the material remained classified.', '07bdd969-9e9b-5567-bdd1-1d0c3de3b705', null, null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('c8c750b1-375f-5d53-9511-52c7c953898f', 'The figures - approximately 129 or 131 active secret underground bases in the United States, approximately 1,477 worldwide, at 17 to 19 billion dollars each - originate in Phil Schneider''s 1995 Preparedness Expo lecture and have no antecedent.', 'f8fa3c7f-7185-5a18-ba9b-c0bf5cf2920a', 'N-SCHNEIDER', null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('4872539c-6856-551c-83b2-c3c908e2f56c', 'The circulating description of an underground city with streets, sidewalks, a lake and its own transit system, and the standing-shadow-cabinet framing, originate in Richard Pollock, ''The Mysterious Mountain'', The Progressive, March 1976, resting on Senate subcommittee material and off-the-record interviews with former officials.', 'dd705501-7987-5de7-a4c2-8f782734570b', 'N-POLLOCK-1976', null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('21922882-c509-5de5-a235-2144e8755f79', 'The template for an American ''vast inhabited underground facility'' narrative - a multi-level cavern world, a hidden population, advanced technology, and a claimant reporting personal experience presented as fact inside a fiction venue - is fixed by Richard Sharpe Shaver''s ''I Remember Lemuria!'', the cover story of Amazing Stories for March 1945, published and promoted as substantially true by editor Ray Palmer.', '2483182c-d84a-5345-9c32-7ac28cd2e006', 'N-SHAVER', null, null, 'unknown'),
  ('67cdea65-e1aa-5fe9-b03c-8c2e11f61973', 'The ''Nekoma pyramid is now a cryptocurrency headquarters'' claim first enters wide circulation from the 26 July 2022 announcement by the office of the Governor of North Dakota, and every consumer-facing version I found descends from it.', '34b09cd6-88c0-5244-aadc-18aee521bcb3', null, null, '2022-07-26', 'inferred'),
  ('e7b44edb-5b0b-57c7-b775-46bdf674366d', 'The commercial framing of decommissioned missile silos as habitable ''castles'', and the associated descriptive vocabulary reproduced across the silo-real-estate and travel corpus, originates with Ed Peden / 20th Century Castles from the mid-1990s.', 'bb184b91-1580-52d2-a380-df14986e1fc6', 'N-20THCENT', null, null, 'unknown')
insert into core.proposition
  (proposition_id, entity_id, class, object_entity_id, claim_id, predicate_args, predicate_key, statement_text, null_code, typology_profile, reference_class, created_by)
values
  ('35203ed2-89d2-5e76-b110-1abb56d99dc5', '6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', 'EXIST', null, null, '{}'::jsonb, 'exist', 'A substantial earth-covered subsurface federal structure designated Building 710 exists on the Denver Federal Center campus.', 'A08', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC1', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('1f366bcf-6711-5d27-87c0-100c2e0618a9', '6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', 'HARDEN', null, null, '{"threats": ["nuclear-weapons-effects (as claimed by unresolved sources; unverified)"]}'::jsonb, 'harden', 'Building 710 was engineered to survive the effects of nuclear attack beyond ordinary construction for a 1960s federal office building.', 'A08', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC1', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('317b66df-e7a5-5f9a-9a94-544790e69edc', '6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', 'FUNCTION', null, null, '{"function": "The structure served as the Defense Civil Preparedness Agency Region 6 emergency operations centre and subsequently as the FEMA Region 8 operations centre."}'::jsonb, 'function', 'The structure served as the Defense Civil Preparedness Agency Region 6 emergency operations centre and subsequently as the FEMA Region 8 operations centre.', 'A08', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC1', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('9f6fd19e-9b48-52db-96b3-573a95fdaf7f', '6b7f49fc-2259-5ae7-99d9-f0a3ee4c8ba7', 'STATUS', null, null, '{"status": "active", "status_basis": "remains in federal use as a FEMA regional operations centre (mapped to core.status_value by the ingest; see README)"}'::jsonb, 'status', 'As of the most recent reporting reaching me, the facility remains in federal use as a FEMA regional operations centre.', 'A08', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC1', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('97c75a2a-04b0-5af9-a790-da6f1de9a881', '4d5e2d74-749b-5c63-ae1a-f5535f9a4cd4', 'EXIST', null, null, '{}'::jsonb, 'exist', 'A two-level subsurface federal structure exists at Denton, Texas, opened in 1964.', 'A10', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('df823842-adee-503e-815d-056083fecadb', '4d5e2d74-749b-5c63-ae1a-f5535f9a4cd4', 'HARDEN', null, null, '{"threats": ["nuclear-weapons-effects (as claimed by unresolved sources; unverified)"]}'::jsonb, 'harden', 'The facility was engineered against nuclear blast effects, including a rated blast door and a stated design overpressure.', 'A10', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('7128468c-08e7-5742-a66b-554a73ba1bd0', '4d5e2d74-749b-5c63-ae1a-f5535f9a4cd4', 'FUNCTION', null, null, '{"function": "The facility served as the federal regional emergency operating centre for its civil-defence region and continues as a FEMA regional operations centre."}'::jsonb, 'function', 'The facility served as the federal regional emergency operating centre for its civil-defence region and continues as a FEMA regional operations centre.', 'A10', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('6fc6a029-d2d3-5626-a7ab-07c1953c46f6', '4d5e2d74-749b-5c63-ae1a-f5535f9a4cd4', 'PROGRAM', null, null, '{"program": "OCDM/DCPA hardened Federal Regional Centers programme", "program_state": "claimed-realised-in-part"}'::jsonb, 'program', 'The Office of Civil Defense and Mobilization planned purpose-built hardened regional centres for all eight of its civil-defence regions, and Denton was the first constructed.', 'A10', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('b367b925-129f-5e47-9d5f-219e9751c86b', '4b87bd09-0843-5042-9b46-a7c6008d005b', 'EXIST', null, null, '{}'::jsonb, 'exist', 'A subsurface federal structure of approximately 120 by 140 feet exists near Bothell, Washington, constructed in 1968.', 'A12', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
  ('0c0f13d6-3f83-5744-a3f9-64ab1d038f32', '4b87bd09-0843-5042-9b46-a7c6008d005b', 'HARDEN', null, null, '{"threats": ["nuclear-weapons-effects (as claimed by unresolved sources; unverified)"]}'::jsonb, 'harden', 'The structure is engineered beyond ordinary construction, with walls and roof of 12 to 36 inches and approximately 450 tons of steel reinforcement.', 'A12', 'unknown-anomaly', 'RC2', 'sweep-01-ingest'),
