  ('45595fc0-7446-5a54-8088-ac842d55e478', '9e20bead-6184-5c84-b159-474254134fe3', 'https://wset.com/archive/the-mystery-of-spears-mountain', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: title and URL only. I could not date it, identify a reporter, or determine its sourcing. Local broadcast journalism, potentially an independent lineage for the Buckingham site, currently an unevaluated pointer.'),
  ('b7f79b22-cd15-5dd3-853b-970b5429f920', 'f68b9079-364f-5a66-b318-2c450b467b46', 'http://wikimapia.org/3707173/AT-T-Hagerstown-2-Project-Office', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: annotation titles and URLs only. CROWD-EDITED and ADVERSARY-WRITABLE under §2.4: these are LEADS and never evidence, and their geometry propagates into downstream renderers by replication, which is one lineage regardless of how many maps show it. Recorded because the annotation set is a useful enumeration of candidate sites, including two (Pottstown PA and Monrovia MD) that I did not develop.'),
  ('9496402a-3be3-56fe-b399-2a05ce907e86', 'bb6cb1e8-7be4-5086-a957-b24a40ef577d', 'https://clui.org/ludb/site/att-chatham-big-hole-site', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: entry titles and search-tool summaries quoting descriptive passages. I INFER: that CLUI conducted site visits and photography. CLUI entries are unsigned and carry no citations in anything I saw, which is why I have assigned P4 (PENDING, treated as T4 per §3.2) rather than P3 despite the organisation''s standing. Critically, CLUI''s framing language on the Project Offices is close enough to LaFrance''s that under the §5.1.7 default it should collapse into his lineage until someone establishes its sourcing.'),
  ('53fb6e23-7088-5444-a85f-6f277d34be7b', '0bf0067e-073b-51f4-b1e7-d6c588515dda', 'https://vitalrecords.com/vri-facilities/roxbury/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: URL and summary text giving two underground floors at 30 and 50 feet below grade and more than 125,000 sq ft of usable space, with tape vaulting and a data centre. SELF-PUBLISHED by the owner-operator; under §2.4 excluded from V. Admissible only as evidence of what the operator asserts, and for the current commercial function which is not in dispute.'),
  ('8e5bc9c6-a23c-5de3-b0ab-88bf332d8e95', '3a5b0a41-cf91-5344-9149-6c11da53d6fa', 'https://coldwar-ct.com/Home_Page_S1DO.html', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | FETCH-BLOCKED] I ATTEMPTED a direct fetch of the Cheshire page and received EGRESS_BLOCKED. I SAW only titles and URLs, plus a summary statement that Cheshire CT reportedly housed an AUTOVON 4-wire switch. Regional Cold War survey sites; P4. Recorded principally as a pointer to two undeveloped candidates (Cheshire CT, Chesterfield) for a later cycle.'),
  ('9ab93153-fb8c-546b-be8a-31f1d74939d5', 'd2e9eb73-3c20-512e-b481-1bb6b2615206', 'https://long-lines.net/places-routes/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | FETCH-BLOCKED] I ATTEMPTED a direct fetch of https://long-lines.net/places-routes/MD01/index.html and received EGRESS_BLOCKED from the network proxy. I SAW only search-result titles and summaries, which carried the Lyons hardening description (blast doors with automatic seal-up system, decontamination shower, gas-turbine engine-alternator, positive-pressure filtered ventilation, 329 ft self-supporting steel lattice tower) and the network-scale figures (100+ main stations, ~1000 repeater vaults, two-week post-attack crew provision). Per the source registry this is P4, a CLLI-keyed compilation, and explicitly a backward-sourcing target: its claims trace to Bell Laboratories Record articles, Bell System Practices and AT&T route maps that should be cited directly.'),
  ('0d55678f-f89b-5699-a314-3b5b4bda4c55', 'c55432d3-bb23-5841-aa3d-a6aa52afa7f6', 'https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/cold-war-bunker-data-center-up-for-sale-in-nebraska/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: title, URL, and summary text giving 54,000 sq ft, circa 1966 construction, a $7.95 million asking price, the listing broker, the street address, and the statement that the building is decommissioned with not all systems functional. I INFER: that the underlying brokerage listing exists and carries a parcel identifier. A broker''s listing is SELF-PUBLISHED with respect to the property''s merits but is third-party with respect to its existence and address.'),
  ('0f3ecefe-9022-5b12-9031-58b6f678a004', 'eca67284-df51-57a4-bbd7-1b1c4d238b62', 'https://nuke.fas.org/guide/usa/c3i/tcs.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: title and URL, and summary material consistent with the L-carrier hardening description. I INFER: standard FAS practice of compiling from open literature. FAS is P3 per the source registry''s anchors. Not read; a .org host I did not attempt to fetch.'),
  ('c912a0b8-912a-54f5-8649-ecab1d1e901d', '0c361a25-04a5-5500-95eb-09073b08e8dd', 'https://computer.rip/2021-12-13-coaxial-goes-to-war.html', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: title, URL and summary text distinguishing hardening classes — that ''Improved'' L-3I was a euphemism for nuclear hardening, that many L-3I facilities were designed for a maximum of about 2 psi overpressure, and that repeater stations every four miles consisted of a buried concrete vault with a sheet-metal surface hut over the manhole. I INFER: nothing further. This is the source that most clearly establishes the MULTIPLE HARDNESS CLASSES point, which is the basis for the second refuted-or-hollow item, and it is a bylined technical blog rather than a primary.'),
  ('ff69f565-6e8f-5a52-9112-e0e3c661aa31', '891e1fb1-a0a3-5830-9fca-b105c3bf010e', 'https://www.qsl.net/n9zia/Nuclear_Design.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P5 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: the page title, URL, and summary text giving the design assumptions — 2.5 miles from a 20-megaton blast, 1000 mph wind, 40 G shock wave, high-velocity debris, intense radiation/heat/electromagnetic effects — and an ''Extremely Hard Design (50 PSI)'' classification. I INFER: that this is a transcription of an AT&T or Bell System engineering document. I could NOT establish what document, and no Bell System Practice number, Bell Laboratories Record citation or accession appeared. This is the origin of the most-copied number on the beat and it currently has no traceable parent. Assigned P5 as an unattributed transcription on a personal page; if the underlying document is identified and resolved, the CONTENT would take a much higher tier while this transcription would remain what it is.'),
  ('ff252026-1856-5928-80d0-b91f3115ef0b', '3b7e9738-601d-532a-8238-09cc43a389a0', 'https://clui.org/ludb/site/att-chatham-big-hole-site', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] I SAW: entry titles and search-tool summaries quoting descriptive passages. I INFER: that CLUI conducted site visits and photography. CLUI entries are unsigned and carry no citations in anything I saw, which is why I have assigned P4 (PENDING, treated as T4 per §3.2) rather than P3 despite the organisation''s standing. Critically, CLUI''s framing language on the Project Offices is close enough to LaFrance''s that under the §5.1.7 default it should collapse into his lineage until someone establishes its sourcing.')
