  ('1ca04498-29dd-5581-82fe-2086059c9912', '68205b1c-1c0a-5af1-919d-3e78d2400ad7', 'https://mdwg.cap.gov/nike-missile-restoration-project', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. SELF-PUBLISHED by the occupying organisation. For the restoration and occupancy claims the author is the claimant; for the site''s Nike history it is a secondary retelling.'),
  ('6fa0ef37-091a-59d2-a5b2-d85340faa0c9', '3eed6745-fad4-5a01-98b9-be4c648a1723', 'https://granite.cap.gov/nike-missile-site', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL, plus summary content on six magazines pumped dry, two restored, and 2023 stabilisation priorities. Same organisation as the item above — ONE lineage under §5.1.1, not two.'),
  ('86edb1c5-37d5-5240-b2ee-91bc3f9ebfaa', '1c251c8b-0323-55f0-8fef-295650d85fbd', 'https://www.thebanner.com/community/local-news/cold-war-nuclear-missiles-nike-baltimore-county-HYLAEIWUDRGI5EYUX255XAJPAQ/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and summary content describing visitors exploring magazines, missile elevators and command rooms, and CAP leasing from the state since 2014. Journalism with physical access — the closest thing to a direct observation I have for this site.'),
  ('5b0b3a00-e227-5c41-a7c9-df1b8026e6f2', '4b2b30bb-bf58-531b-bcd1-1fd83231242d', 'https://www.baltimoresun.com/2018/06/11/off-limits-exploring-a-long-abandoned-nike-missile-site-in-annapolis/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, date. NOTE: this piece is about the ANNAPOLIS-area site (W-25 Davidsonville), not BA-79. Recorded here because it surfaced in the same sweep and because conflating the two Maryland sites is an easy and consequential error. Kept as a cross-reference, not as support for BA-79.'),
  ('465c1f17-17ee-5936-b0a2-b784992f9ddc', '1f90dd2c-b9b7-5257-885c-44f6fd54cfa2', 'https://ed-thelen.org/W-25MerleColeDavidsonvilleMarylandAirDefense.pdf', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: URL and title. A named scholarly article on Maryland Nike air defense, hosted on the Thelen register. It concerns W-25, not BA-79, but is the best-quality secondary in the Maryland Nike cluster and is a transparent-compiler candidate. SOURCE-REGISTRY flags acute succession risk on ed-thelen.org — Ed Thelen died in 2024 — and recommends mirroring now. Endorsed.'),
  ('29e2de62-004e-5a5f-9d53-c395464dad36', '7a39da5d-d559-57cf-b32f-e276078004f4', 'https://mde.maryland.gov/programs/land/marylandbrownfieldvcp/documents/davidsonville%20nike%20launch%20and%20control.pdf', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P1 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: URL and document title in a result block. A state environmental regulator''s brownfields/VCP document for the W-25 Davidsonville Nike launch and control site — again W-25, not BA-79. Recorded because it demonstrates the record class that exists for this whole population and is reachable in principle: state VCP files describe former launch areas in physical detail, for the regulator''s own purposes, entirely independently of any enthusiast compilation.'),
  ('8fed422c-1f9b-5ba4-9490-918cfefad4d4', 'f28ee1f2-e82a-5c2b-86cb-5ac67f481f56', 'https://www.history.nd.gov/historicsites/minutemanmissile/oscarzerohistory.html', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P1 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: titles, URLs and summary content on 1965 completion, Minuteman II installation, START removal and silo filling, and preservation of the above-ground blast door. A state agency describing property it owns — the issuing authority for STATUS and CONTROL. Not fetched.'),
  ('b6695a37-f285-5abb-88b0-4aa3da0b3b26', 'c0172cc8-b4b8-58e7-8e34-93977528964b', 'https://sah-archipedia.org/buildings/ND-01-GG3', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL and the entry identifier ND-01-GG3 as it appeared in the result URL. A Society of Architectural Historians scholarly survey entry. Recording the identifier as seen in the URL; I have not verified it resolves to this content.'),
  ('7d6aaebe-4b31-5fc6-9253-469910562ae9', '43eb8b0d-dc71-56c1-b6c8-1ee5bff55124', 'https://oscarzero.wordpress.com/thehistoricsite/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. Same compiler as the RSL entry above — SAME LINEAGE for anything it asserts across both candidates, and must not be counted twice.'),
  ('ba8f56c4-525e-5ce9-b873-b9cf19f141c0', '9bf8bb07-3419-5e35-889d-46aa25e47338', 'https://minutemanmissile.com/afbwing6.html', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. Enthusiast compilation of Minuteman wing organisation.'),
  ('b73f9f18-df18-5904-b3a3-4f42e956207d', '6e0032fc-3e54-5cbf-820c-f4e834c52266', 'https://www.afmissileers.org/321-MG', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. SOURCE-REGISTRY rates the AAFM newsletter archive CRITICAL and P3: free, bulk-downloadable, published by the veterans'' own association, with unit-to-site mappings and the ''Taps for Missileers'' column giving squadrons and duty locations. It is the preferred route for missile-personnel attestation and I could not reach it.'),
  ('6bd22833-b12a-5f7c-a82a-37b5c2c26de7', 'bdb491e2-2166-5359-b43b-8a9a1c182613', 'https://www.armscontrol.org/act/2001-09/last-minuteman-iii-missile-silo-destroyed', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and a summary stating the last Minuteman III silo slated for dismantlement under START I, at Grand Forks AFB, was destroyed on 24 August 2001. Specialist arms-control journalism with direct access to treaty data exchanges.'),
  ('e5f8604d-dee4-5de6-a41c-300cbadbc6bb', '482333a9-aff0-586d-83e7-12a0a2f01270', 'https://www.armscontrol.org/act/1999-11/first-150-minuteman-iii-missile-silos-destroyed', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. Gives the population figure of 150 and the 1999 start of destruction.'),
  ('2a311a77-8054-5403-9305-d6bf8f722a20', '70714f6e-55fc-502d-92d1-da01427e41af', 'https://www.nps.gov/articles/endingthearmsrace-start.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P1 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL and summary content on the destruction method, the 20-foot excavation, the observation cone and the 90-day verification period. NPS interprets the Minuteman Missile National Historic Site and is a federal agency, though not the issuing authority for treaty implementation. Not fetched — .gov egress blocked.'),
  ('bdac668d-6788-51e6-a631-3c4279f7bfdc', 'ff405ac1-f5c8-5efe-bc8b-ec30bddec4e9', 'https://nuke.fas.org/control/start2/text/convers.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P2 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. INFER: a hosted copy of treaty text governing conversion and elimination procedures. This is a MIRROR of a treaty instrument, and under §2.6/CAP-6 a grade resting on a mirror-only receipt caps at B until the issuing authority resolves.'),
  ('1f8b1f5a-43c2-5d30-9ed2-083d0babde86', '591a3cbd-f92d-5566-aaf3-e30d0b3702b8', 'https://grandforksherald.com/news/2083942-missile-sites-sale', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and summary content reporting GSA auctions with bids above $6,000 and a high of $17,800 for a launch control facility, and naming ''India-Zero'' as one of 15 MAFs. Local journalism on a public auction; the auction record itself is the acquisition target.'),
  ('1544ef61-c899-5c43-919e-e5307e65f61d', 'e2d9f947-06b3-5a55-8fc3-158c52ddd483', 'http://www.themilitarystandard.com/missile/minuteman/destruction.php', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and summary content on ~800 lb explosive charges and the controlled two-metre door displacement. Domain confirmed EGRESS_BLOCKED on a sibling page. Unsourced enthusiast compilation — the operational detail is plausible and needs an independent primary.'),
  ('997316c3-7920-52e5-87b2-95abe8937683', 'cdb403a1-5da6-5dee-b2ed-bebae9c8a93c', 'https://www.krqe.com/news/new-mexico/cold-war-era-missile-silo-in-new-mexico-transformed-into-air-bnb/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and summary content naming Gary Baker as owner and host, reporting two silos bought ~25 years ago at $55,000 each, and a change of plan from museum to short-term rental. Local broadcast journalism relaying the owner''s account.'),
  ('e9e19421-189c-535b-9c5b-9fed808b6661', '1ac7e45e-b797-5ac7-abeb-bfb1717436c0', 'https://www.thefabricator.com/thefabricator/blog/shopmanagement/staying-overnight-in-a-cold-war-era-missile-silo-near-roswell-part-1-1', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: titles and URLs for a two-part first-person account by a trade-magazine writer who stayed on site. A bylined direct observation with lawful access — genuinely useful raw material for A1-alt and for §5.4 custody, since a byline in a named publication is exactly the custody path the rule requires.'),
  ('3f212789-200d-568f-873e-576daf87ec86', 'b52a35fc-0d0d-5480-a37c-d85cb3c1641f', 'https://www.atlasmissilesilo.com/documents_atlasf_579th.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: two URLs from this domain, one of them explicitly a documents index for the 579th SMS. INFER: an enthusiast register hosting SCANNED PRIMARY DOCUMENTS. If those documents are individually retrievable this is a transparent compiler and the primaries become the lineages. This is the highest-value unchecked source in this entry.'),
  ('3fe27528-94a6-5bcd-88eb-9fbe898f731b', 'd6128ea3-8558-5e54-9272-7b9893898f3c', 'https://www.wafbmuseum.org/history-of-walker-air-force-base/579th-missile-squadron/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. A local institutional museum with a collection relating to Walker AFB — a third, independent root for the unit history.'),
  ('304282a5-d7c7-5fdc-b1cc-af14185c363f', 'd8373813-eff5-56d0-b551-de6b6e5a7e38', 'https://www.579sms.com/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: domain in a result block. A squadron veterans'' association site; the class SOURCE-REGISTRY recommends for unit-to-site mapping and for personnel attestation.'),
  ('7adecae8-215d-5e4f-ae10-aab4c73c39e7', '6590a5ee-1865-559d-a35e-8da6554374fd', 'http://www.astronautix.com/w/warrenafb.html', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. A long-standing compiled encyclopaedia of launch and missile deployment data; unsourced at the point of use.'),
  ('2da6333d-d978-535c-b8db-2112b08520cb', '5567a937-81f6-5ee5-9d06-3dccbfd6ee48', 'https://afmissileers.org/Atlas-D', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title and URL. The veterans'' association''s own page. SOURCE-REGISTRY rates the AAFM newsletter run CRITICAL/P3 and notes it is free, bulk-downloadable and carries first-person Atlas operational accounts — the vernacular record for exactly this question of what the coffin launchers were actually like.'),
  ('00edf64e-88ad-5668-ad2c-07f9e0ba94a4', '6c188307-dc1a-58b5-9721-39d9df89ace7', 'https://www.themilitarystandard.com/missile/atlas/atlas-d/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P4 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: title, URL, and summary content describing the coffin configuration, the missile stored above ground horizontally, semi-hard facilities and limited protection. Domain confirmed EGRESS_BLOCKED on a sibling page. Unsourced enthusiast compilation.'),
  ('26334a72-f918-5ac4-b99e-bb38a3db01f1', '2ff68ae9-07fd-5a70-ac42-0f40dd260bc4', 'https://www.atlasmissilesilo.com/564SMS/index.htm', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: URLs for both squadron sections. Same domain as the 579th documents index — potentially a transparent compiler hosting scanned primaries, unchecked.'),
  ('ebcdff62-8f45-5e90-b5ab-534246c4ea22', 'c1afdf91-97b6-5ecd-96eb-4828afac7462', 'https://www.565sms.com/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P3 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] SAW: domain in a result block. Squadron veterans'' association; the preferred route for personnel attestation per SOURCE-REGISTRY.'),
  ('58a08c1e-95b5-511c-a74b-937023edca5a', 'be8bb770-a4c1-54a0-9653-b798f3e93f56', 'https://coreinsightsintl.com/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P5 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] Named in the cog beat''s refuted_or_hollow record: pages re-presenting publicly documented FEMA regional centres as concealed installations; unbylined; the lineage is the Sauder/Schneider deep-underground-military-base corpus.'),
  ('01dc4d33-46ee-5acb-a06b-27bec1ab6130', 'bc561ef9-2cbd-5b49-83ff-2704cc0b871a', 'https://deepundergroundmilitarybases.com/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P5 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] Named in the cog beat''s refuted_or_hollow record and surfaced again on the silo beat; same corpus recirculating; adds no identifier, record or observation to the public material it restyles.'),
  ('ab6b4541-bc0f-5aaa-ae4c-6185fcfeb8fe', 'cbfff9f9-dec5-507c-a7cd-03f90d126039', 'https://silo.tips/', 'UNRESOLVED', 'code', '[P5 | SEARCH-SNIPPET-ONLY] Named in the silo beat''s refuted_or_hollow record: the claim that decommissioned Atlas/Titan/Nike sites are entrances to a national DUMB network is ''an accretion onto a claim structure that predates it'' — the Sauder/Schneider material.')
