  ('317b66df-e7a5-5f9a-9a94-544790e69edc', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary earth-bermed or partially below-grade federal office building of late-1960s design on a large federal campus, whose Cold War name reflects the agency that happened to occupy it rather than any protective engineering. This null is genuinely strong: the Denver Federal Center is a sprawling multi-building campus assembled from a wartime ordnance plant, and it contains a great deal of unremarkable government construction. What would distinguish it: the NRHP nomination''s statement of significance, or the USACE design record, specifying a design overpressure, blast closures, shielding or CBR filtration. What would NOT distinguish it: earth cover, reinforced concrete, absence of windows, a generator, or the building''s Cold War-era name. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('9f6fd19e-9b48-52db-96b3-573a95fdaf7f', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary earth-bermed or partially below-grade federal office building of late-1960s design on a large federal campus, whose Cold War name reflects the agency that happened to occupy it rather than any protective engineering. This null is genuinely strong: the Denver Federal Center is a sprawling multi-building campus assembled from a wartime ordnance plant, and it contains a great deal of unremarkable government construction. What would distinguish it: the NRHP nomination''s statement of significance, or the USACE design record, specifying a design overpressure, blast closures, shielding or CBR filtration. What would NOT distinguish it: earth cover, reinforced concrete, absence of windows, a generator, or the building''s Cold War-era name. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('97c75a2a-04b0-5af9-a790-da6f1de9a881', 'A10', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A10 — a federal office building whose below-grade levels carry a civil-defence fallout-shelter designation and nothing more, with ''bunker'' being a local honorific applied to an ordinary basement. This null is weakened, though not excluded, by the 13-ton door: fallout-shelter designation required shielding mass, not blast closures, and licensed shelter space in ordinary basements was enormously common. What would distinguish it: the door''s engineering rating, or an OCD construction contract as opposed to an OCD shelter-survey licence. What would NOT distinguish it: being underground, thick walls, ventilation equipment, a generator, or a shelter sign. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('df823842-adee-503e-815d-056083fecadb', 'A10', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A10 — a federal office building whose below-grade levels carry a civil-defence fallout-shelter designation and nothing more, with ''bunker'' being a local honorific applied to an ordinary basement. This null is weakened, though not excluded, by the 13-ton door: fallout-shelter designation required shielding mass, not blast closures, and licensed shelter space in ordinary basements was enormously common. What would distinguish it: the door''s engineering rating, or an OCD construction contract as opposed to an OCD shelter-survey licence. What would NOT distinguish it: being underground, thick walls, ventilation equipment, a generator, or a shelter sign. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
