  ('7831a8b5-9fd1-5bbb-b79b-0ec679099f07', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary partially below-grade federal office building whose ''bunker'' description is retrospective, with fallout-shelter-grade rather than blast-grade protection. Massachusetts has a dense population of genuine Cold War hardened sites (the Hadley PACCS facility, Nike sites, Air Force stations), and the regional habit of calling any government structure with earth on it a bunker is strong. What would distinguish it: a construction record with a protective specification, or the 1969 handover documentation showing what was actually built. What would NOT distinguish it: roof antennas (every regional emergency office has them), being underground, or proximity to Boston. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('90310f23-8eeb-5d5e-847d-7d1d19f47726', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary below-grade federal regional office with severe-weather protection, built in an era when civil-defence construction had already moved away from blast hardening. This null is strengthened, not weakened, by the facility''s own reported description. A secondary null worth naming is A06 (storage): a 37,734 sq ft subterranean structure with independent utilities is an equally good records or materiel store. What would distinguish it: a construction specification, a DCPA design record, or the parcel''s real-property CATCODE. What would NOT distinguish it: acreage, square footage, independent utilities, being subterranean, or the presence of communications equipment. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('920db968-3d06-57dd-844d-f1add2c9ad1e', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary below-grade federal regional office with severe-weather protection, built in an era when civil-defence construction had already moved away from blast hardening. This null is strengthened, not weakened, by the facility''s own reported description. A secondary null worth naming is A06 (storage): a 37,734 sq ft subterranean structure with independent utilities is an equally good records or materiel store. What would distinguish it: a construction specification, a DCPA design record, or the parcel''s real-property CATCODE. What would NOT distinguish it: acreage, square footage, independent utilities, being subterranean, or the presence of communications equipment. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('1a678305-f1cf-5163-8208-bcff978aaca1', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary below-grade federal regional office with severe-weather protection, built in an era when civil-defence construction had already moved away from blast hardening. This null is strengthened, not weakened, by the facility''s own reported description. A secondary null worth naming is A06 (storage): a 37,734 sq ft subterranean structure with independent utilities is an equally good records or materiel store. What would distinguish it: a construction specification, a DCPA design record, or the parcel''s real-property CATCODE. What would NOT distinguish it: acreage, square footage, independent utilities, being subterranean, or the presence of communications equipment. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('e8bd376f-35d2-50d7-8612-e0f09c193c9a', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 — a decommissioned Second World War naval munitions magazine, subsequently reused for federal offices and communications, whose subterranean and reinforced character is entirely inherited from its ordnance-storage origin. This null is DOCUMENTED, not merely available: the naval air station and its magazine are independently attested in California military-post histories and in a state water-board cleanup document for the former NAAS. Under BES 4.6 a documented null is the condition for null_state = DOMINANT. What would distinguish the civil-defence claim: an OCD conversion contract, an FCC or NTIA assignment at the coordinate, or filtration and shock-isolation plant. What would NOT distinguish it: concrete thickness, earth cover, doors, remoteness, or the parcel''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
