  ('7cb34936-02dc-512c-ad87-9bc2ab6f4e4b', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 — a decommissioned Second World War naval munitions magazine, subsequently reused for federal offices and communications, whose subterranean and reinforced character is entirely inherited from its ordnance-storage origin. This null is DOCUMENTED, not merely available: the naval air station and its magazine are independently attested in California military-post histories and in a state water-board cleanup document for the former NAAS. Under BES 4.6 a documented null is the condition for null_state = DOMINANT. What would distinguish the civil-defence claim: an OCD conversion contract, an FCC or NTIA assignment at the coordinate, or filtration and shock-isolation plant. What would NOT distinguish it: concrete thickness, earth cover, doors, remoteness, or the parcel''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('797e9934-ef28-521f-9b28-60f5d1663db3', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 — a decommissioned Second World War naval munitions magazine, subsequently reused for federal offices and communications, whose subterranean and reinforced character is entirely inherited from its ordnance-storage origin. This null is DOCUMENTED, not merely available: the naval air station and its magazine are independently attested in California military-post histories and in a state water-board cleanup document for the former NAAS. Under BES 4.6 a documented null is the condition for null_state = DOMINANT. What would distinguish the civil-defence claim: an OCD conversion contract, an FCC or NTIA assignment at the coordinate, or filtration and shock-isolation plant. What would NOT distinguish it: concrete thickness, earth cover, doors, remoteness, or the parcel''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('1a990ce0-5096-5941-9c1e-7b4320cf30a2', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 combined with A08 — a multi-phase federal parcel comprising a 1950s civil-defence training school and a decommissioned Nike battery, later reused as ordinary federal support offices, in which the ''underground bunker'' is the Nike magazine complex plus a hardened communications room rather than a purpose-built continuity facility. This null is unusually strong here because the site demonstrably had at least two prior federal uses that independently produce subsurface reinforced structures. What would distinguish the COG reading: DCPA-era construction documentation for the 1970s underground work, or NAWAS operational records naming Olney as the alternate control point. What would NOT distinguish it: subsurface concrete (Nike produces it), antennas, guarded access, or the site''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('fe8f7e35-183b-5a51-bca2-f70bb10d680b', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 combined with A08 — a multi-phase federal parcel comprising a 1950s civil-defence training school and a decommissioned Nike battery, later reused as ordinary federal support offices, in which the ''underground bunker'' is the Nike magazine complex plus a hardened communications room rather than a purpose-built continuity facility. This null is unusually strong here because the site demonstrably had at least two prior federal uses that independently produce subsurface reinforced structures. What would distinguish the COG reading: DCPA-era construction documentation for the 1970s underground work, or NAWAS operational records naming Olney as the alternate control point. What would NOT distinguish it: subsurface concrete (Nike produces it), antennas, guarded access, or the site''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
