  ('a6389c95-b054-5071-afbd-7d665b96a332', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 combined with A08 — a multi-phase federal parcel comprising a 1950s civil-defence training school and a decommissioned Nike battery, later reused as ordinary federal support offices, in which the ''underground bunker'' is the Nike magazine complex plus a hardened communications room rather than a purpose-built continuity facility. This null is unusually strong here because the site demonstrably had at least two prior federal uses that independently produce subsurface reinforced structures. What would distinguish the COG reading: DCPA-era construction documentation for the 1970s underground work, or NAWAS operational records naming Olney as the alternate control point. What would NOT distinguish it: subsurface concrete (Nike produces it), antennas, guarded access, or the site''s federal ownership. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('073aa58d-f112-530b-a089-fab9bad62cb2', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08/A06 — a genuine USDA agricultural research station and former cavalry remount depot, on which the State Department was an ordinary co-located federal tenant occupying some surface buildings for contingency office space, with no concealment and no hardening. This null accounts for every reported physical fact: the buildings, the stockpile, the communications station, even the highway improvements (Warren County sits on the Skyline Drive corridor and had independent reasons for road investment). What would distinguish the concealment reading: a State Department, GSA or interagency record describing the arrangement, or an emergency-relocation designation document naming the site. What would NOT distinguish it: federal ownership, remoteness, distance from Washington, the presence of a radio station, or the site''s later Smithsonian use. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('ef1bcd9b-8b1a-5331-9700-821048b22f7e', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08/A06 — a genuine USDA agricultural research station and former cavalry remount depot, on which the State Department was an ordinary co-located federal tenant occupying some surface buildings for contingency office space, with no concealment and no hardening. This null accounts for every reported physical fact: the buildings, the stockpile, the communications station, even the highway improvements (Warren County sits on the Skyline Drive corridor and had independent reasons for road investment). What would distinguish the concealment reading: a State Department, GSA or interagency record describing the arrangement, or an emergency-relocation designation document naming the site. What would NOT distinguish it: federal ownership, remoteness, distance from Washington, the presence of a radio station, or the site''s later Smithsonian use. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
