  ('1bf57266-b0ab-5e50-9cb1-037ceb5f861a', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — an ordinary large above-ground federal office complex in a converted historic hospital building, which is what it visibly is. For the EXIST and CONTROL propositions there is no meaningful contest and the null and the claim agree. The mundane alternative BITES only against HARDEN, where it wins outright. What would distinguish a hardening claim if anyone made one: protective specifications in the 1954 conversion records or in any later modification. What would NOT distinguish it: the building''s size, its federal ownership, its civil-defence occupancy, or the presence of communications facilities. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
