  ('7ca14db7-273b-57b5-a69e-f4589031638b', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — an AT&T long-haul microwave and switching station, hardened in the 1960s to DoD''s AUTOVON survivability specification, which since divestiture has become an ordinary piece of AT&T network real estate and which in 2016 the company wanted to expand into a conventional carrier data centre, on a mountaintop it already owned, in the county that hosts more data-centre capacity than anywhere on earth. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT: the 2016 file itself — a data-centre build has a named electrical service agreement with Dominion, a cooling design, a raised-floor or rack layout and a stated IT load, all of which appear in commission-permit engineering exhibits; a hardened federal build has none of those and instead has shielding, filtration and berthing. Second discriminator: the Loudoun parcel and deed chain — a federal leasehold, easement or restrictive covenant on an AT&T fee parcel is unusual and would be visible. Third: whether the 1960s structure carries any NTIA federal frequency assignment as distinct from AT&T''s FCC licences. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
