  ('a11cfb23-d349-5c98-9c6a-4b63850467e8', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 / A12 — a decommissioned AT&T troposcatter relay of a well-documented Cold War type, obsolete, sold off, and now a private house with a very unusual basement. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from a facility with a continuing role: the deed chain and current assessment record, both public in Buckingham County, plus the simple fact that a residence and a classified facility cannot occupy the same footprint. Here the mundane alternative is probably the truth about the present, and the live question is only about 1958–2000. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('d5b908a7-23b8-59bb-b98a-e4f7a1d7f15a', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — a 1968 telephone-company operations building, built underground because AT&T''s network survivability doctrine of the period called for it, containing no government function whatever, and since 1995 an ordinary commercial records warehouse. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from something more: any federal tenancy, lease or contract, which would appear in FPDS or in a recorded lease; and any indication that the 1968 build was federally funded or specified, which would appear in AT&T''s own corporate record. On present evidence the mundane alternative is very probably the complete truth and the register should say so rather than treating the building''s undoubted hardness as though hardness implied a secret. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('d8a12f51-8b2c-5f6c-ace6-2b241fe2e73e', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — a 1968 telephone-company operations building, built underground because AT&T''s network survivability doctrine of the period called for it, containing no government function whatever, and since 1995 an ordinary commercial records warehouse. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from something more: any federal tenancy, lease or contract, which would appear in FPDS or in a recorded lease; and any indication that the 1968 build was federally funded or specified, which would appear in AT&T''s own corporate record. On present evidence the mundane alternative is very probably the complete truth and the register should say so rather than treating the building''s undoubted hardness as though hardness implied a secret. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
