  ('802f64d4-4c99-5ea4-9328-ce9ef8746daa', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — a 1968 telephone-company operations building, built underground because AT&T''s network survivability doctrine of the period called for it, containing no government function whatever, and since 1995 an ordinary commercial records warehouse. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from something more: any federal tenancy, lease or contract, which would appear in FPDS or in a recorded lease; and any indication that the 1968 build was federally funded or specified, which would appear in AT&T''s own corporate record. On present evidence the mundane alternative is very probably the complete truth and the register should say so rather than treating the building''s undoubted hardness as though hardness implied a secret. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('51f477ca-18fb-54f1-aefc-c9dcac7f31f9', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — a Bell System L-4 coaxial main station, one of over a hundred, hardened to the network-wide standard of its route class because AT&T hardened the whole L-4 build, carrying ordinary commercial long-distance traffic alongside government traffic, decommissioned when the technology died and now a distressed commercial property. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from something more: nothing found so far suggests anything more, and the register should say that. The one thing that would change the picture is documentation of a site-specific hardening class above the route standard, or a federal tenancy — neither of which any source claims. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
