  ('acc686ab-e86b-5bf9-9529-b8627ef014b4', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — a Bell System L-4 coaxial main station, one of over a hundred, hardened to the network-wide standard of its route class because AT&T hardened the whole L-4 build, carrying ordinary commercial long-distance traffic alongside government traffic, decommissioned when the technology died and now a distressed commercial property. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT from something more: nothing found so far suggests anything more, and the register should say that. The one thing that would change the picture is documentation of a site-specific hardening class above the route standard, or a federal tenancy — neither of which any source claims. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('53e4f600-84e5-58bf-abb7-08a0a12cdce6', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07 — an AT&T Long Lines equipment building, hardened to whatever the route standard was, sold off when the microwave network was retired, rebuilt with a multi-million-dollar investment as an ordinary commercial colocation facility whose marketing leans on its Cold War provenance because that is a selling point in the disaster-recovery market. WHAT WOULD DISTINGUISH IT: the Boone County deed chain (was any grantor a federal entity?), an FCC ASR and ULS history for the tower (was the licensee ever anyone but AT&T?), and any instance-level engineering document. All three are checkable and all three point the same way on present evidence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
