  ('475b0e1e-996a-5afd-a86e-bd02232222ba', 'A12', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A12 — a decommissioned Strategic Air Command command post, genuinely hardened for its original purpose, subsequently and undramatically reused first for federal records storage and then as an academic library depository, with no continuing continuity-of-government role and no currency hoard. This null is not merely available, it is documented and it is the majority reading in the sources themselves. For the historical propositions the null and the claim substantially agree; the null bites only against the currency claim and against any suggestion of continuing COG use. What would distinguish the currency claim: a Federal Reserve facility or transport record. What would NOT distinguish it: the tunnel, the blast doors, the mountain, the Federal Reserve''s documented records-storage tenancy, or the site''s undisputed military past. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
