  ('aa7c93f3-f7b9-554f-9ab3-81840eabfd4a', 'A07', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A07/A08 in combination - a very large civil airport, built over budget in the early 1990s, whose automated baggage system failed catastrophically and left walled-off concrete voids. What would distinguish a concealed hardened facility from that: a structural floor-loading filing, a blast-door or blast-valve line item in a Denver building-department record, a NEPA document specifying CBR filtration or shielding, or a real-property record showing a federal custodial entity for space beneath the terminal. None retrieved, and per BES 6.1 their absence here is genuinely informative rather than routine, because a municipal airport is not a classified-construction authority and its permit record is not structurally withheld. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
