  ('3a7a55bf-c2b3-55ef-8bc6-65a09bc4574f', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A11 for the network, and for the underlying documents nothing mundane is needed at all - they are what they appear to be. The specific alternative to a melted transcontinental tunnel is: a cancelled 1970s civil-tunnelling R&D programme funded partly by the National Science Foundation for civil applications, plus the genuinely large body of real US deep-underground construction that already has names and records - the Rainier Mesa U12 tunnel complex at the Nevada Test Site being the clearest example, where six nuclear weapons-effects tests were conducted in the U12t tunnel alone between 1970 and 1987, with drifts, a portal, a tailings pile and a published DOE historical evaluation. What would distinguish: any portal, any alignment, any spoil accounting, any procurement trace. None exists in the lineage. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
