  ('bc16202d-8535-5642-8586-72e04e17f40d', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A11 combined with a documented 1930s Los Angeles treasure-hunting boom: a mining engineer with an unvalidated instrument, a county willing to take a share of a hypothetical find at no cost to itself, and a metropolitan newspaper with an appetite for the story. What would distinguish a real subsurface city from that: any artefact, any void encountered by the shaft, any later encounter during the extensive regrading and construction that has since occurred across Fort Moore Hill - a century of downtown excavation constitutes an enormous accidental search with an entirely negative result. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
