  ('cdd7ac25-2e57-52e9-b07d-450272013af0', 'A02', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A02, a commercial mine and solution-cave system in Mojave limestone, plus A11 for the treasure content specifically. What would distinguish: any assay, any survey, any sonar or geophysical return consistent with a 3000-foot cavern and a flowing river, or any independent visitor''s account of the described chamber. Ninety years have produced none. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
