  ('f7a48826-f3ce-57f5-a332-1015e61193ae', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 plus A11 in combination: real Cold War and post-Cold-War federal emergency contingency planning, some of it genuinely alarming and genuinely documented, whose actual products are plans and authorities rather than buildings - overlaid with a later accretion of constructed underground facilities for which no record of any class exists. What would distinguish: MILCON lines, NEPA filings, FRPP entries, county deeds, or spoil. The planning half leaves exactly the records planning leaves; the construction half leaves none. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
