  ('3c20ea83-0cdc-5708-af64-c5604ef83d81', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A11 in its literary form: a pulp magazine serial written by a claimant and promoted as fact by an editor with a circulation incentive, which the sources describe as having roughly doubled reader engagement and drawn over 2,500 letters. What would distinguish a real cavern civilisation from that: literally any physical trace. None has ever been offered, in eighty years, by anyone. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('6d39addf-0af9-5f25-b48e-d37bf71ef3ea', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/HRDN there is no mundane alternative worth naming — this is A01/A12 territory and both fail immediately; the structure is a photographed landmark. The live nulls are on the modern propositions. For FUNC(operating data centre): A07, ''an announced but substantially unbuilt commercial data-centre project, with a small pilot deployment used to keep an incentive package and a purchase option alive.'' What would distinguish it: an interconnection agreement or a filed load study with the serving cooperative showing contracted MW at the site; a county building permit with a valuation; property-tax assessment change reflecting installed equipment; an FCC/state utility filing; PeeringDB or IP-transit route announcements originating at the site. What will NOT distinguish it: the company''s own press release, the governor''s press release, a photograph of the exterior, or the number ''$500 million''. For CTRL(Bitzero): A09/A11-adjacent — ''a signed agreement that has not closed, or has closed only in part'' — distinguished by the Cavalier County recorder''s deed index and nothing else. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
