  ('2200bfb7-5df8-55ef-b4c5-c0ca0d106978', 'A08', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A08 — ''an ordinary above-ground government radar installation with no hardening beyond weather and physical-security requirements.'' Distinguished by: the original Safeguard hardening design criteria (a Corps of Engineers or Army Safeguard System Command design record), an EMP-hardening specification in the MIL-STD-188-125 lineage cited in any modernisation procurement, or a DD Form 1391 with hardening scope for the upgrade work. Photographs of a large concrete building do not distinguish it — that is squarely on the universal-D0 list. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
