insert into core.alternative_disposition
  (proposition_id, null_code, is_selected, disposition, reasoning, assessed_by)
values
  ('8aa4e3e6-cf91-5ec9-942b-4d56357416ab', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST: A01 fails outright — there are photographs and a ticketed tour. The interesting null is on HRDN/EXTN: A05, ''a hardened-looking but shallow launcher and equipment vault, whose depth and blast rating are described from memory and marketing rather than from drawings.'' Distinguished by: the Safeguard RSL as-built drawings (Corps of Engineers / Army Safeguard System Command), or the GSA disposal description, which for surplus federal property routinely recites structures and dimensions because a buyer needs them. That GSA description is the cheapest high-value document on this candidate. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
