  ('e0d39d6a-c7f1-5112-9192-166f8316ff5f', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST: A01 fails outright — there are photographs and a ticketed tour. The interesting null is on HRDN/EXTN: A05, ''a hardened-looking but shallow launcher and equipment vault, whose depth and blast rating are described from memory and marketing rather than from drawings.'' Distinguished by: the Safeguard RSL as-built drawings (Corps of Engineers / Army Safeguard System Command), or the GSA disposal description, which for surplus federal property routinely recites structures and dimensions because a buyer needs them. That GSA description is the cheapest high-value document on this candidate. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('219d3fff-d496-5ebf-b274-17da39c99287', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/CTRL there is no serious null. The null that matters is on the FEAT/FUNC(cosmic-ray laboratory) proposition: A06 — ''an underground space used for ordinary storage or residence, to which a research use has been retrospectively or loosely attached, or which was attached to a DIFFERENT silo in the same ring.'' This is the live risk: my only source for the cosmic-ray use is a single Adirondack Explorer feature, and the search summary itself wavered between attributing it to Site 5 (Lewis) and to the Au Sable Forks site 556-6. Distinguished by: a published physics paper or technical report naming the site as its counting location, an SUNY Plattsburgh institutional record, or an equipment-siting document. A magazine sentence does not distinguish it and I am not going to pretend otherwise. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
