  ('8fad68ee-8560-5803-8c7e-5736a81dc511', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/CTRL there is no serious null. The null that matters is on the FEAT/FUNC(cosmic-ray laboratory) proposition: A06 — ''an underground space used for ordinary storage or residence, to which a research use has been retrospectively or loosely attached, or which was attached to a DIFFERENT silo in the same ring.'' This is the live risk: my only source for the cosmic-ray use is a single Adirondack Explorer feature, and the search summary itself wavered between attributing it to Site 5 (Lewis) and to the Au Sable Forks site 556-6. Distinguished by: a published physics paper or technical report naming the site as its counting location, an SUNY Plattsburgh institutional record, or an equipment-siting document. A magazine sentence does not distinguish it and I am not going to pretend otherwise. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('79bc9bf6-642a-5948-90b4-58978f2fcca6', 'A06', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A06/A10 — ''a converted Atlas F silo fitted out to a high domestic standard and marketed as a survival shelter, whose protective performance is asserted by the seller and has not been certified against any published standard.'' This is not a hostile framing; it may well be an excellent building. What would distinguish the marketing claim from an engineering fact: a filed structural or blast analysis, a permit valuation with engineered scope, an EMP-shielding test report in the MIL-STD-188-125 lineage, or a third-party engineer''s report. What would NOT distinguish it: photographs, floor counts, amenity lists, the original 1961 Air Force design hardness (which describes the ORIGINAL structure in its ORIGINAL condition, not a building modified over fifteen years), or press coverage of any volume. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
