  ('721a96d1-4c65-5165-9cfd-2328885a5089', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST: none survives — these are mapped, regulated, physically entered structures. The live null is on STAT and FEAT: A12, ''a decommissioned facility of an already-known typology, largely flooded, partially collapsed, and hazardous, whose interior condition is described from irregular urban-exploration visits rather than from survey.'' What would distinguish a documented condition from an anecdotal one: the CDPHE/USACE site assessment reports and monitoring-well data, which by their nature describe access, structural condition and water levels; a county coroner''s or fire department''s incident report; an engineering condition survey. Photographs from a trespass visit do not distinguish it. Note that this null is not really a competitor — it is close to the truth — which is why the interesting propositions here are about condition, contamination and status rather than existence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
