  ('37f70c62-8e86-529a-8d94-34240370e3b7', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/TYPO: A12 — ''a decommissioned facility of a different, already-known typology'', specifically an ordinary former Army administrative post whose ''magazines'' are surface storage buildings rather than subsurface missile magazines. This sounds pedantic and is not: the distinguishing feature of a Nike LAUNCH site is the underground magazine with its missile elevator, and many former Nike parcels retain only the control-site buildings while the launch area was filled or sold separately. What would distinguish it: the Army site list''s launch/control site split for BA-79; the state property record''s description; HAER documentation, since many Nike sites were HAER-recorded with measured drawings deposited at the Library of Congress; or a photograph of an elevator in a magazine. Reports of tours ''inside cavernous magazines with metal elevators'' are direct-observation support and are the strongest thing I have. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('86ca746d-8de7-5c93-99f3-a75789d6dc1f', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/TYPO: A12 — ''a decommissioned facility of a different, already-known typology'', specifically an ordinary former Army administrative post whose ''magazines'' are surface storage buildings rather than subsurface missile magazines. This sounds pedantic and is not: the distinguishing feature of a Nike LAUNCH site is the underground magazine with its missile elevator, and many former Nike parcels retain only the control-site buildings while the launch area was filled or sold separately. What would distinguish it: the Army site list''s launch/control site split for BA-79; the state property record''s description; HAER documentation, since many Nike sites were HAER-recorded with measured drawings deposited at the Library of Congress; or a photograph of an elevator in a magazine. Reports of tours ''inside cavernous magazines with metal elevators'' are direct-observation support and are the strongest thing I have. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('daaa3fa7-d7d4-5eeb-958b-cf241927e484', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/STAT the live null is A12/A10 — ''a launch facility that was destroyed by the standard START method and subsequently reconstructed or re-presented as intact for interpretive purposes, i.e. a museum reconstruction rather than a preserved original.'' This is not a cynical hypothesis: it is exactly what happened at many sites, where a surface presentation sits over a destroyed duct. What would distinguish them: the START elimination notifications and the US inventory of eliminated launchers, which enumerate WHICH launchers were destroyed; the transfer instrument from the Air Force to the state; a structural condition survey. An intact-looking blast door at ground level does NOT distinguish them — a closed door over a gravel-filled duct is precisely what the null predicts, and my own sources describe the duct as filled. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('586dbbac-28b3-5b37-a9a8-dd346a3239ff', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/STAT the live null is A12/A10 — ''a launch facility that was destroyed by the standard START method and subsequently reconstructed or re-presented as intact for interpretive purposes, i.e. a museum reconstruction rather than a preserved original.'' This is not a cynical hypothesis: it is exactly what happened at many sites, where a surface presentation sits over a destroyed duct. What would distinguish them: the START elimination notifications and the US inventory of eliminated launchers, which enumerate WHICH launchers were destroyed; the transfer instrument from the Air Force to the state; a structural condition survey. An intact-looking blast door at ground level does NOT distinguish them — a closed door over a gravel-filled duct is precisely what the null predicts, and my own sources describe the duct as filled. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('a24c3cdf-803e-50bc-8263-40936804190f', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/STAT the live null is A12/A10 — ''a launch facility that was destroyed by the standard START method and subsequently reconstructed or re-presented as intact for interpretive purposes, i.e. a museum reconstruction rather than a preserved original.'' This is not a cynical hypothesis: it is exactly what happened at many sites, where a surface presentation sits over a destroyed duct. What would distinguish them: the START elimination notifications and the US inventory of eliminated launchers, which enumerate WHICH launchers were destroyed; the transfer instrument from the Air Force to the state; a structural condition survey. An intact-looking blast door at ground level does NOT distinguish them — a closed door over a gravel-filled duct is precisely what the null predicts, and my own sources describe the duct as filled. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('4fae475f-6b91-5e4f-95a4-9b28ba2f3699', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For EXIST/STAT the live null is A12/A10 — ''a launch facility that was destroyed by the standard START method and subsequently reconstructed or re-presented as intact for interpretive purposes, i.e. a museum reconstruction rather than a preserved original.'' This is not a cynical hypothesis: it is exactly what happened at many sites, where a surface presentation sits over a destroyed duct. What would distinguish them: the START elimination notifications and the US inventory of eliminated launchers, which enumerate WHICH launchers were destroyed; the transfer instrument from the Air Force to the state; a structural condition survey. An intact-looking blast door at ground level does NOT distinguish them — a closed door over a gravel-filled duct is precisely what the null predicts, and my own sources describe the duct as filled. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('f3012330-bd28-52b4-acb5-24199872d049', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For STAT(destroyed) the named null is A11-adjacent and is worth stating because it is a live folk belief rather than a straw man: ''the silos were not really destroyed; missiles remain emplaced or the facilities were quietly retained.'' What would distinguish it: the START elimination notifications and the ninety-day open-excavation verification regime itself, which was DESIGNED as the discriminator — the whole point of leaving a hole open for three months is that a concealed retention is not possible under overhead observation; plus GSA conveyances and county deeds transferring the parcels to private persons who now farm them. What would NOT distinguish it: aerial imagery of a fenced square in a field, which is equally consistent with a demolished site, a retained site and a private buyer''s fence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('c75742ca-f127-5ea0-8495-320aaea109e5', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For STAT(destroyed) the named null is A11-adjacent and is worth stating because it is a live folk belief rather than a straw man: ''the silos were not really destroyed; missiles remain emplaced or the facilities were quietly retained.'' What would distinguish it: the START elimination notifications and the ninety-day open-excavation verification regime itself, which was DESIGNED as the discriminator — the whole point of leaving a hole open for three months is that a concealed retention is not possible under overhead observation; plus GSA conveyances and county deeds transferring the parcels to private persons who now farm them. What would NOT distinguish it: aerial imagery of a fenced square in a field, which is equally consistent with a demolished site, a retained site and a private buyer''s fence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
