  ('3bd29083-d6f8-505c-ae7e-79d917502364', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For STAT(destroyed) the named null is A11-adjacent and is worth stating because it is a live folk belief rather than a straw man: ''the silos were not really destroyed; missiles remain emplaced or the facilities were quietly retained.'' What would distinguish it: the START elimination notifications and the ninety-day open-excavation verification regime itself, which was DESIGNED as the discriminator — the whole point of leaving a hole open for three months is that a concealed retention is not possible under overhead observation; plus GSA conveyances and county deeds transferring the parcels to private persons who now farm them. What would NOT distinguish it: aerial imagery of a fenced square in a field, which is equally consistent with a demolished site, a retained site and a private buyer''s fence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)')
insert into core.alternative_disposition
  (proposition_id, null_code, is_selected, disposition, reasoning, assessed_by)
values
  ('ee0025f0-696c-570e-996f-ba67e21e4b1a', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'For STAT(destroyed) the named null is A11-adjacent and is worth stating because it is a live folk belief rather than a straw man: ''the silos were not really destroyed; missiles remain emplaced or the facilities were quietly retained.'' What would distinguish it: the START elimination notifications and the ninety-day open-excavation verification regime itself, which was DESIGNED as the discriminator — the whole point of leaving a hole open for three months is that a concealed retention is not possible under overhead observation; plus GSA conveyances and county deeds transferring the parcels to private persons who now farm them. What would NOT distinguish it: aerial imagery of a fenced square in a field, which is equally consistent with a demolished site, a retained site and a private buyer''s fence. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('da515d56-1751-5cc7-a371-0011ee7a38be', 'A06', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A06 — ''a former Atlas F site converted to an ordinary residence and let as a novelty short-term rental, whose protective and dimensional claims are hospitality marketing.'' What would distinguish a genuine hardened conversion: county permits with engineered scope, a structural report, or the original Corps of Engineers as-built showing what was retained. What would NOT distinguish it: listing photographs, guest reviews, or a description of the blast door — a blast door that has been welded open, propped, or bypassed by a new stair is a photograph of hardening, not hardening. This is a general point about converted silos and I would like it stated once, here, and reused: THE ARTEFACT OF HARDENING SURVIVES THE FUNCTION OF HARDENING, and the register should refuse to let a photograph of a 1961 door carry a 2026 HARDEN proposition. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('91f59c31-9bd7-5a85-93c8-cf37affb7730', 'A06', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A06 — ''a former Atlas F site converted to an ordinary residence and let as a novelty short-term rental, whose protective and dimensional claims are hospitality marketing.'' What would distinguish a genuine hardened conversion: county permits with engineered scope, a structural report, or the original Corps of Engineers as-built showing what was retained. What would NOT distinguish it: listing photographs, guest reviews, or a description of the blast door — a blast door that has been welded open, propped, or bypassed by a new stair is a photograph of hardening, not hardening. This is a general point about converted silos and I would like it stated once, here, and reused: THE ARTEFACT OF HARDENING SURVIVES THE FUNCTION OF HARDENING, and the register should refuse to let a photograph of a 1961 door carry a 2026 HARDEN proposition. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('895f61d4-6ec0-55e3-9241-6c804898d347', 'A06', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A06 — ''a former Atlas F site converted to an ordinary residence and let as a novelty short-term rental, whose protective and dimensional claims are hospitality marketing.'' What would distinguish a genuine hardened conversion: county permits with engineered scope, a structural report, or the original Corps of Engineers as-built showing what was retained. What would NOT distinguish it: listing photographs, guest reviews, or a description of the blast door — a blast door that has been welded open, propped, or bypassed by a new stair is a photograph of hardening, not hardening. This is a general point about converted silos and I would like it stated once, here, and reused: THE ARTEFACT OF HARDENING SURVIVES THE FUNCTION OF HARDENING, and the register should refuse to let a photograph of a 1961 door carry a 2026 HARDEN proposition. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('d2dc38d6-c2cc-5d9e-9f8d-193ffe0cf692', 'A06', true, 'selected-strongest', 'A06 — ''a former Atlas F site converted to an ordinary residence and let as a novelty short-term rental, whose protective and dimensional claims are hospitality marketing.'' What would distinguish a genuine hardened conversion: county permits with engineered scope, a structural report, or the original Corps of Engineers as-built showing what was retained. What would NOT distinguish it: listing photographs, guest reviews, or a description of the blast door — a blast door that has been welded open, propped, or bypassed by a new stair is a photograph of hardening, not hardening. This is a general point about converted silos and I would like it stated once, here, and reused: THE ARTEFACT OF HARDENING SURVIVES THE FUNCTION OF HARDENING, and the register should refuse to let a photograph of a 1961 door carry a 2026 HARDEN proposition. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
  ('20647975-df8b-5af7-8502-e4a1f36a6fcf', 'A11', true, 'selected-strongest', 'Inverted here, and that is the point. The usual null for this register is ''this is not really hardened''. For Atlas D the null is essentially TRUE BY DESIGN — A05/A08, ''an above-ground equipment shelter with a movable roof, protecting against weather and providing dispersal, not against blast.'' What would distinguish any genuine hardening claim: an Air Force design criteria document stating an overpressure rating for the coffin launcher. I expect such a document exists in the AFWL/AFSWC technical-report lineage and would show a low figure. Nothing I have seen asserts otherwise, and the phrase ''limited protection'' recurs. | null_state as graded: SURVIVING. DERIVED per 4.6, and VACUOUS. A named null is present so the state is not UNTESTED; DOMINANT requires the null to be affirmatively documented by a verified T1/T2 row and none exists; INSUFFICIENT and EXCLUDED require verified rows in V at D2+/D3+ and V is empty. SURVIVING therefore holds only because the null trivially accounts for all zero rows in V. This must not be read as a finding that the mundane explanation is strong.', 'claude-opus-5 (W1 grading pass)'),
